│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     I made a small fix in `fastapi/_compat/v2.py`, but I did not confirm it resolves issue #14247, so treat it as a partial fix.               │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     **What changed:** `get_flat_models_from_model` used `known_models = known_models or set()`, which discards a caller-supplied empty set and │
│ starts a new one. It now only creates a fresh set when `known_models is None`.                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     **What I checked:**                                                                                                                        │
│     - Two reproductions with a nested model containing a `computed_field` (one with a nested `Sub` in both the request body and the response,  │
│ one with `Sub` only in the response) both produced correct separate `Sub-Input` and `Sub-Output` schemas. So I found no reproduction of the    │
│ nested-model bug.                                                                                                                              │
│     - `tests/test_separate_openapi_schemas.py` ran zero tests, so the change has no test coverage. I did not add tests, per the rules.         │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     **Not done:** I did not identify the real root cause of the 0.119.0 regression. The likely candidate is the `flat_model_fields`            │
│ construction in `get_definitions`, which always builds nested-model fields in validation mode, but I did not confirm that. The patch is        │
│ submitted with `patch_size` 612 and `files_changed` 1.                                                                                         │
